  "body": "The proposer misread the rule. The rule as written names the kernel `conformance.kernel.grounding` (\"conformance.kernel.grounding: The harness's grounding verdict for a value, its cited span and the document, no relaxation, value-in-span checked: the input is one JSON object {\\\"value\\\", \\\"span\\\", \\\"document\\\"}; GROUNDED, SPAN_MISSING, SPAN_NOT_IN_DOCUMENT or VALUE_NOT_IN_SPAN\"), but the proposal committed to `open:creib.forge.conformance.oracle._grounding_kernel`, an internal function name that the harness does not expose. The execution failed with `MINI_OPEN_KERNEL_NOT_FOUND: 'oracle' has no '_grounding_kernel'`, so the rule as written and the code do not part company; the proposer used the wrong kernel identifier. Next, build a proposal that uses the documented kernel `conformance.kernel.grounding` (e.g. `open:creib.forge.conformance.kernel.grounding` in the commitment) and keep the same rewrite.",
